<span id="Description"></span>
==Popis==

Příkaz [[Image:Part_RefineShape.svg|24px]] '''Part Upravit tvar''' vytváří z vybraných objektů [[Glossary/cs#Parametric|parametrické]] kopie s vylepšeným tvarem. Odstraňuje z rovinných a válcových ploch zbytečné hrany.

[[File:PartRefineShape_it.png]]
{{Caption|Originál s 11 plochami (vlevo) a vylepšená kopie se 7 plochami (vpravo).}}

<span id="Usage"></span>
==Použití==

# Vyberte jeden nebo více objektů.
# Z menu vyberte možnost {{MenuCommand|Díl → Kopírovat → [[Image:Part_RefineShape.svg|16px]] Vylepšit tvar}}.
# Pro každý objekt se vytvoří vyčištěná parametrická kopie
# Původní objekty jsou skryté.

<span id="Notes"></span>
== Poznámky ==

* Many [[Part_Workbench|Part]] objects and [[PartDesign_Workbench|PartDesign]] features have a {{PropertyData|Refine}} property. Setting that property to {{TRUE}} is preferable over using this command as it avoids an extra object.
* By default this command creates [[Glossary#Parametric|parametric]] copies. There is a [[Fine-tuning|fine-tuning]] parameter to change this to [[Glossary#Non-parametric|non-parametric]] copies.
* This command can be used after [[Part_ShapeFromMesh|converting a mesh to a shape]].
* Refining an object may prevent 3D printers from printing unwanted edges once the object is exported to a mesh format.
* Some interesting information about what is happening with placement and how to access by Python can be found in this [https://forum.freecad.org/viewtopic.php?t=77568#p675456 forum post].

==Properties==

See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].

A Part RefineShape object is derived from a [[Part_Feature|Part Feature]] object and inherits all its properties. It also has the following additional property:

===Data===

{{TitleProperty|Refine}}

* {{PropertyData|Source|Link}}: specifies the linked source shape.

==Scripting==

The Python command for refining a shape is the following:

{{Code|code=
shape.removeSplitter()
}}


